item.body:
Closes #300
Claim: mac/w6-session-wire-opus (2026-10-28)

Not a lot: app wiring of LOT-044 (#70) into LOT-081's accounts. No `LOTS.md` change.

**Problem.** The app checked restored account sessions with the placeholder `LocalSessionCheck`, which only read the jar. A session HFR no longer accepted stayed "restored" and failed later, silently. Nothing was ever retried.

**Cause.** LOT-081 shipped before LOT-044's `SessionRefreshFlow` was merged.

**What changed.**
- `ForumSessionCheck` (`AccountServices.swift`) runs `SessionRefreshFlow.refresh` behind an app-side `SessionRefreshing` protocol, because the flow's probe seam is internal to `HFRClient`. It maps the outcomes as follows:
  - `valid` → `valid`, persisted as before;
  - `expired(.noIdentityCookie)` → `expired`: the existing LOT-081 re-login from the row and the account menu;
  - every `unconfirmed`, and `.cancelled` → `unconfirmed`: the row is `restored` and the session is kept;
  - any other `NetworkError` → `failed`: the row shows "forum injoignable" and the session is kept.

  Only a jar without identity logs out. `AccountsModel.live()` uses this check. `LocalSessionCheck` is deleted, and previews use a check that sends nothing.
- **Quiet re-check.** `SwiftHFRApp` calls `AccountsModel.recheckUnconfirmedSessions(now:)` when the scene becomes active.
  - It checks again only `restored` and `checkFailed` accounts, and keeps their row status while it runs.
  - It runs at most once per 5 min after the last check, and never while another re-check or a restore (the launch check) runs.
  - A result applies only if the account still has the same session and status, so a login or a removal during the check wins.
  - A `valid` write-back is dropped if a login was saved meanwhile (`loginSaves` count).
- **Why this wide:** the issue's scope only. There is no engine change and no new HFR fact (HFR-PROTOCOL untouched). There is no new pending capture: LOT-044's #281, #282 and #283 stay open, and stale cookies stay `unconfirmed` until #281 lands.
- **Docs:**
  - `LOT-081` spec section "#300 — forum session check wiring";
  - `CHANGELOG-LEGACY` row **33**: legacy checked at launch only and had no failure callback (`HFRplusAppDelegate.m:150`, `MultisManager.m:280-293`). Rows 31 and 32 belong to #332 and #318.

**Tests**
- `App/SwiftHFRTests/Accounts/ForumSessionCheckTests.swift`. `ScriptedRefresher` answers with the outcomes LOT-044's capture-backed tests proved, and expires identity-less jars itself, as the flow's step 1. The tests:
  - `everyFlowOutcomeMapsToItsCheckResult`;
  - `transportFailuresAreFailedAndCancellationIsUnconfirmed`;
  - `liveFlowExpiresJarsWithoutIdentityAndKeepsTheirCookies`: the real flow behind a `CapturedForum` that answers nothing, and nothing is sent;
  - `launchCheckConfirmsReportsAndNeverLogsOut`;
  - `recheckRetriesOnlyUnconfirmedSessionsAfterTheInterval`;
  - `recheckDuringTheLaunchCheckSendsNothingMore`;
  - `recheckWhileTheLaunchCheckWaitsOnAnotherAccountSendsNothing`;
  - `secondRecheckWhileOneRunsSendsNothing`;
  - `loginDuringARecheckWinsOverItsResult`;
  - `loginSavedWhileACheckWritesBackWinsOverItsCookies`.
- `App/SwiftHFRTests/Accounts/CapturedSessionCheckTests.swift` drives the same model through the real `SessionRefreshFlow` on committed LOT-001 captures (`R55-p1`, `W00`, `R12`, `W17c`, `R01`), and nothing is sent. The tests:
  - `capturedProfilePageConfirmsTheSessionAndPersistsItsRefresh`;
  - `staleCookieStandInsKeepTheSessionLoggedIn`;
  - `unknownPagesKeepTheSessionLoggedIn`;
  - `networkErrorsAreReportedAndKeepTheSession`;
  - `recheckAfterANetworkErrorConfirmsOnTheCapturedProfilePage`.
- **Shown to fail without the change.** The author ran these mutations, and the Fable review of #309 ran them again on an iPhone 18 Pro, iOS 27.0 simulator:
  - `unconfirmed` mapped to `expired`;
  - the former local rule;
  - network errors mapped to `expired`;
  - no `.cancelled` case;
  - no re-check interval;
  - no restore or re-check guard;
  - no same-status guard;
  - no login-save count.

  The LOT-081 spec says which other mutations are traced only.

**Reviews:**
- Fable APPROVE at 192edc3 by `ext/bybifok-opus-1`, with 5 findings. Findings 1–4 are fixed in b2e83ff and d11232d; finding 5 needs no change.
- Steward Fable delta review: APPROVE at b2e83ff, plus 2 doc findings, fixed in d11232d.

Coordination: `SwiftHFRApp.swift` is also touched by #303. This PR adds one `.onChange(of: scenePhase)`.

